    "eli5": "Computers on the internet don't understand names like `google.com` or `netflix.com`\u2014they only understand numerical coordinates called **IP addresses** (like `142.250.190.46` or `2607:f8b0:4005::200e`).\n\n**DNS (Domain Name System)** is the decentralized global contact book of the internet. Whenever you type a URL, your computer asks a chain of specialized servers to translate that human-friendly name into the server's numerical IP address in a fraction of a second.",
